## Coverage and Completeness

- `property_coverage_months.data_complete = true` — the only source of truth for whether a month has complete data
- Coverage window floor = `owner_pm_relationships.start_date` — never the first booking date
- Zero-booking months within PM tenure = `data_complete = true` (valid covered data)
- Future months never receive `data_complete = true`
- All period queries must check `property_coverage_months` before computing metrics
- Evaluate `data_complete` **per property** — one property's cross-month booking must never affect another property's completeness

### Case 1 / Case 2 — upload completeness logic (Row 179)

Evaluated per property on upload (`app/dashboard/upload/page.tsx`) and on dashboard load re-evaluation (`lib/coverage-completeness.ts`).

**Case 1 — definitively closed (set `data_complete = true` immediately on upload):**
- Among bookings overlapping the month, the latest checkout crosses into a future month, AND
- `upload_date >= that booking's check_in date` (guest already checked in — cancellation risk gone)

**Case 2 — may still have open bookings (wait for calendar to close):**
- Latest checkout falls within the month being evaluated, OR
- Latest checkout crosses the boundary but `upload_date < check_in date`
- Set `data_complete = true` only when `CURRENT_DATE >= first day of following month`

**Re-evaluation pass:** On dashboard load, re-evaluate rows where `data_complete = false` and the calendar month has closed — flip Case 2 months without requiring re-upload.

**Rendering rule (never lock, always degrade):** Once `CURRENT_DATE >= first day of the following month`, render the month regardless of `data_complete`. Portfolio-level soft note only on dashboard and analytics pages:
`"Booking data for [Month YYYY] may not be up to date — upload a new file to refresh."`

### Schema v0.19 — submarket zip lookup

- **`submarket_zip_codes`** — maps `market_id` + `zip_code` → AirDNA `submarket_id`
- **`properties.airdna_submarket_id`** — resolved from `properties.zip` via lookup; NULL falls back to market-level benchmark
- **`market_benchmarks.submarket_id`** — NULL = market-level row; non-null = submarket-level row

